#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: ggdef
# doc: migrated from tests/fixtures/tuple_literal_resource_value.gg (run_gg pair)
# expect:
#   exit: 0
#   stdout: "3\n42\n"
#!end
# Regression: Tuple literal with resource-typed element in a bare-init
# context. `(Vector[int], int) p = ([1, 2, 3], 42)` pre-fix failed
# typecheck with `expected Vector[int], found int[3]` because TupleLiteral
# inferred each element type without reading decl_type_hint.
#
# Parallel to dict_literal_resource_value.gg's typecheck side: container
# literals (Dict, Tuple) must propagate per-element type hints from the
# declared type so nested collection literals coerce correctly.
#
# Fix: TupleLiteral typecheck reads decl_type_hint when it's a Tuple of
# matching arity, sets each element's decl_type_hint to the corresponding
# declared element type before recursive infer.
void main():
    (Vector[int], int) p = ([1, 2, 3], 42)
    print(p.0.len())   # expected: 3
    print(p.1)         # expected: 42
